definition:
n something that is lost or surrendered as a penalty; 
n a penalty for a fault or mistake that involves losing or giving up something
n the act of losing or surrendering something as a penalty for a mistake or fault or failure to perform etc.

v. be a regular or frequent visitor to a certain place
a. coming at short intervals or habitually
s. frequently encountered;

a. Of or pertaining to Gascony, in France, or to the Gascons;
   also, braggart; swaggering.
n. A native of Gascony; a boaster; a bully. See Gasconade.
